One pass does it. Set the running maximum to element zero, walk the rest of the array, and swap in any value that beats the incumbent. O(n) time, O(1) extra space, and you can't do better — nothing can be declared the maximum until every element has been looked at.

```python
def find_max(arr):
    m = arr[0]
    for x in arr[1:]:
        if x > m:
            m = x
    return m
```

I pointed that same scan at the only array of results I keep. Argentina held the running max for a moment, Saudi Arabia displaced it 2-1 at Lusail, Indonesia displaced that 2-0 in Jakarta. Final return value: Indonesia, greater than Argentina at soccer, settled in a single sweep.
